Relationship Between JVM, JRE and JDK

JVM: Executes Java bytecode.

JRE: Provides JVM and runtime libraries.

JDK: Provides development tools along with the runtime environment.

JDK⊃JRE⊃JVM

Note: This is the traditional conceptual relationship. Modern Java distributions (Java 9 onwards) do not necessarily provide a separate bundled JRE.

